  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "text": "In a supermarket we have various sections like vegetables, fruits, cleaning products, and so on.",
      "refs": ["Q0000"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "text": "Each section contains related products.",
      "refs": ["Q0001"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C3",
      "text": "By the same token, a class in Java contains related functions.",
      "refs": ["Q0002"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C4",
      "text": "Now, every Java program should have at least one class that contains the main function.",
      "refs": ["Q0003"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C5",
      "text": "Can you guess the name of that class?",
      "refs": ["Q0004"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C6",
      "text": "It's main.",
      "refs": ["Q0005"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C7",
      "text": "We start with a class keyword, then we give our class a proper descriptive name, and then we add a pair of curly braces.",
      "refs": ["Q0007"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C8",
      "text": "Now the functions that we define in between these curly braces belong to this class, and more accurately we refer to them as methods.",
      "refs": ["Q0008"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C9",
      "text": "So a method is a function that part of a class.",
      "refs": ["Q0009"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C10",
      "text": "In some languages like python, we can have a function that exists outside of a class, so we call it a function, but when a function belongs to a class we refer to it as a method of that class, okay?",
      "refs": ["Q0010"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C11",
      "text": "Now in Java, all these classes and methods should have an access modifier.",
      "refs": ["Q0011"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C12",
      "text": "An access modifier is a special keyword that determines if other classes and methods in this program can access these classes and methods.",
      "refs": ["Q0012"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C13",
      "text": "We have various access modifiers like public, private, and so on.",
      "refs": ["Q0013"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C14",
      "text": "Now most of the time we use the public access modifier, so we put that in front of our class and method declarations.",
      "refs": ["Q0014"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C15",
      "text": "So this is the basic structure.",
      "refs": ["Q0015"],
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "related_refs": []
    }
  ],
